  "releaseNotes": "11.0.0\n\n* New: a net11.0 build, for .NET 11. The net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 builds stay. The major version\n  is 11 because it follows the .NET generation.\n* Now on Com.H.Threading.Scheduler 11.0.x, which changes what happens to a task whose handler\n  throws: it is tried again after a pause instead of on every tick, and a task that used up its\n  retry_attempts_on_error runs again at its next scheduled time. If you relied on a failing task\n  being tried again every second, set sleep_on_error to your tick interval. The scheduler's notes\n  list every change: https://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H.Threading.Scheduler/11.0.0#releasenotes-body-tab\n* Fixed: SchedulerServiceOptions.ValueProcessors had no effect. The processors are now used, and\n  one with the name of a built-in processor replaces it.\n* New: SchedulerServiceOptions.DefaultSleepOnError sets the pause for a failed task that has\n  neither sleep_on_error nor an interval (the scheduler's default is 60 seconds).\n* Dependencies: Com.H 11.0.x, and Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection and\n  Microsoft.Extensions.Options 10.0.11 or later (they were 8.0.0 or later).",
